    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "S\nSYDNEY\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nAUSTRALIA can provide the visitor with a range of experiences from attending cultural events in the\nSydney Opera House, pictured here, to visiting aboriginal tribes in the Outback. This continent, as\nlarge as the United States, encompasses many aspects; The Great Barrier Reef, marvelous skiing in\nJuly just 200 miles south of Sydney; bountiful gems and strange animals and birds. Unique flora and\nfauna are here in marvelous abundance. Pan Am serves Sydney and Melbourne from Los Angeles\nSan Francisco, New York, London, Auckland, Honolulu, and Nadi.\nNAM.",
      "Fist Class Menus\nManhattan\nTom Collins\nCanadian\nLibationso\nSherry\nDubonnet Campari\nGin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nVodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nGin Vodka Rum Premium Beer\nCoffee\nDelectationso\nDelice Neptune\nCold water shrimp and lush snow crab in a flavorful dressing on a bed of crisp greens.\nFilet Mignon Maître d'Hôtel\nSelect grilled tenderloin steak with a savoury herb butter.\nServed with mousseline potato and broccoli florets Mimosa.\nChicken Suprême Teriyaki\nDelicate breast of chicken in a soy-ginger sauce with pineapple\nServed with steamed white rice and oriental vegetable sauté.\nCoupe Romanoff\nRich vanilla sherbet in a tart strawberry sauce\ngarnished with walnuts and a mound of sweet whipped cream.\nServed with rich butter cookies\nTea\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nSelected Red and White Wines\nChampagne Brut\nDrambuie Benedictine Crème de Menthe\nCognac Napoléon Contreau\nKahlúa\nAmaretto di Saronno\nD.4335\n2001.080.022"
    ],
